From 499f1c4601ad39942fd1b2204053a387bec9b989 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cyril Hrubis <metan@ucw.cz>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:44:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] parse: don't dereference the end of the token vector in
 calc()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

css__parse_calc_value() peeks the token it is about to parse and, unless it
is a '(', switches on token->type — but parserutils_vector_peek() returns
NULL at the end of the vector. Unfinished expression e.g. 'calc(1px*'
crashes the parser here.

The other three functions in the group (calc_sum, calc_product,
calc_number) all check for the NULL; only this one assumed a token.

The three test entries are all of that same shape: an operator, then the end
of the sheet. The truncation has to happen inside a NESTED block —
'@media all{* {' and no closing brace — or the parser never gets far enough.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Cyril Hrubis <metan@ucw.cz>
---
 src/parse/properties/utils.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/parse/properties/utils.c b/src/parse/properties/utils.c
index 9e4ef08..1528ed3 100644
--- a/src/parse/properties/utils.c
+++ b/src/parse/properties/utils.c
@@ -1867,6 +1867,10 @@ css__parse_calc_value(css_language *c,
 
 	/* On entry, we are already pointing at the value to parse, so peek it */
 	token = parserutils_vector_peek(vector, *ctx);
+	if (token == NULL) {
+		return CSS_INVALID;
+	}
+
 	if (tokenIsChar(token, '(')) {
 		parserutils_vector_iterate(vector, ctx);
 		consumeWhitespace(vector, ctx);
-- 
